/*
 * Synagraphic — Neon Glow Enhancement (EXAMPLE / REFERENCE)
 *
 * Copy `glow.css` from this folder to a location on your machine,
 * then follow the steps below to enable it in VS Code.
 *
 * REQUIREMENTS:
 *   Install "Custom CSS and JS Loader" by be5invis:
 *   https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=be5invis.vscode-custom-css
 *
 * SETUP:
 *   1. Copy glow.css somewhere stable on your machine, e.g.:
 *        C:\Users\YourName\vscode-custom\synagraphic-glow.css   (Windows)
 *        ~/vscode-custom/synagraphic-glow.css                   (macOS/Linux)
 *
 *   2. Add to VS Code settings.json:
 *        "vscode_custom_css.imports": [
 *          "file:///C:/Users/YourName/vscode-custom/synagraphic-glow.css"
 *        ]
 *
 *   3. Open Command Palette (Ctrl+Shift+P / Cmd+Shift+P):
 *        > Enable Custom CSS and JS
 *
 *   4. Restart VS Code when prompted.
 *
 * NOTES:
 *   - VS Code may show a "corrupted installation" warning — this is expected.
 *     Run "Disable Custom CSS and JS" to restore a clean state at any time.
 *   - Works with all 6 Synagraphic themes. Glow intensity adapts per theme.
 *   - Admin/sudo may be required on some systems for the CSS loader to write files.
 */
